// Every function is lifted with the target's default C calling convention.  A
// Ghidra prototype model that places arguments differently is reported: a
// warning by default, an error under -strict.  On ARM the default model is
// `__stdcall` (AAPCS); `__thiscall`, `unknown` and an absent convention do not
// contradict it.  `__stdcall_softfp` passes floating-point arguments in core
// registers and is not the default.
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -print-tu -output %t > %t.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=WARN %s --input-file %t.log
// RUN: test -e %t.cir
// RUN: not %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -strict -output %t.strict > %t.strict.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=ERR %s --input-file %t.strict.log
// RUN: test ! -e %t.strict.cir
//
// WARN: Diag Warning: {{.*}}lossy lift [callconv-unsupported]: calling convention '__stdcall_softfp' of function 'ext_softfp' is not the default for arm; lifted with the target default convention
// WARN-NOT: Diag Error
// WARN-NOT: of function 'callconv_unsupported'
// WARN-NOT: of function 'ext_default'
// WARN-NOT: of function 'ext_this'
// WARN-NOT: of function 'ext_unknown'
// WARN-NOT: of function 'ext_absent'
//
// ERR: Diag Error: {{.*}}lossy lift [callconv-unsupported]: calling convention '__stdcall_softfp' of function 'ext_softfp'
// ERR-NOT: of function 'ext_default'
// ERR: Skipping code generation due to prior diagnostics errors
